# TLS passthrough routing table.
#
# Install as /etc/haproxy/passthrough.conf. This file is NOT tracked in the
# repository — it names your own hostnames and internal ports, which are yours,
# not this project's.
#
# One line per domain:
#
#   <sni-hostname>    <backend-target>    [options]
#
# Options (optional, any number, space-separated after the target):
#
#   proxy-protocol      Send PROXY protocol v2 to the backend, so it can see the
#                       real client IP instead of HAProxy's. In TCP mode HAProxy
#                       opens a new connection to the backend, so without this
#                       the backend sees 127.0.0.1 for every request.
#                       The backend MUST be configured to accept it — and once
#                       it is, connecting to it directly stops working.
#   proxy-protocol-v1   The older text format, for backends that only speak v1.
#   cloudflare-only     Only Cloudflare's edge ranges may connect to this SNI;
#                       anyone else is silently dropped. For a proxied (orange
#                       cloud) record whose origin must not be reachable
#                       directly.
#   terminate           Decrypt here and re-encrypt to the backend, instead of
#                       passing the handshake through. Behind Cloudflare, plain
#                       passthrough only ever sees the edge's address — the real
#                       client is in CF-Connecting-IP, inside the TLS stream.
#                       With terminate + proxy-protocol the backend receives the
#                       real client in the PROXY header, as the hub's own
#                       domains do. HTTP(S)/WebSocket/gRPC only, and HAProxy
#                       needs a certificate for the domain (domains.map).
#
# Connections whose TLS SNI matches the hostname are handed to the target with
# the handshake untouched, so that service keeps terminating its own TLS. The
# hub's own domains are unaffected; anything matching neither is silent-dropped.
#
# After editing, apply with:
#
#   sudo /opt/notification-hub/bin/passthrough.sh sync
#
# which regenerates HAProxy's map and backend files, validates the result, and
# reloads with no dropped connections.

# domain                     target                  options
#servenet.example.com        127.0.0.1:441
#mooz.example.com            127.0.0.1:440
#node.example.com            127.0.0.1:442           proxy-protocol
#cdn.example.com             127.0.0.1:443           terminate proxy-protocol cloudflare-only
